        "factor": "Forecast anchor around 12% for near-term risk (non-zero baseline), with new signals likely to nudge probability upward",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Baseline forecasts place non-trivial risk; new signals justify moving probability higher within the horizon."
      }
    ],
    "synthesis_rationale": "Calibrated posterior of 0.58 results from multiplying the upward pushes from concrete CS findings, elevated intelligence signals, and battlefield escalation against attribution uncertainty and the nonzero baseline. The factors are treated as moderately correlated (widely reported signals) and the final interval reflects plausible calibration around the posterior."
  }
}

